records.qn_text:
(a) whether Government has undertaken initiatives to improve tourism infrastructure at UNESCO World Heritage Sites and major pilgrimage destinations in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of projects approved;
(c) the details of funds allocated; and
(d) the measures being taken to promote sustainable tourism?

(a) whether Government has undertaken youth development and volunteer programmes in Maharashtra under NYKS and related Central schemes;
(b) the number of youth clubs covered during the last three years;
(c) the funds allocated and utilised; and
(d) the impact of these initiatives on youth leadership, community participation and skill development?

(a) whether Government has reviewed skill development programmes implemented in Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise number of youth trained under Central schemes during the last three years;
(c) the placement rate achieved; and
(d) the steps taken to align skill training with industry requirements?

(a) whether Government has undertaken measures to improve coastal shipping and inland water transport connectivity in Maharashtra;
(b) the projects sanctioned during the last three years;
(c) the funds allocated and utilised; and
(d) the expected benefits in reducing logistics costs and promoting sustainable transport?

(a) whether Government has modernised warehouses and storage facilities in Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of new storage capacity created;
(c) the funds allocated and utilised during the last three years; and
(d) the measures taken to minimise post-harvest losses and improve food security?

(a) whether the Central Government has undertaken cluster development programmes for MSMEs in the State of Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of clusters sanctioned;
(c) the financial assistance provided; and
(d) the employment generated and exports promoted through these clusters?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of metro rail projects in the State of Maharashtra;
(b) the details of projects under implementation, city-wise;
(c) the cost escalation, if any, reported during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure timely completion and improved urban mobility?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to strengthen cyber security infrastructure and digital literacy in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of cyber awareness programmes and cyber security projects implemented;
(c) the funds allocated; and
(d) the measures adopted to protect citizens and Government institutions against cyber threats?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the availability of quality seeds, fertilizers and agricultural mechanisation support to farmers in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of subsidies and assistance provided;
(c) whether any shortages were reported during the last three years; and
(d) the corrective measures taken to ensure timely supply of agricultural inputs?

(a) whether Government has strengthened passport services in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of Passport Seva Kendras established in the State during the last three years;
(c) the number of passports issued there; and
(d) the measures taken to reduce the processing time?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the development of major and minor ports in Maharashtra, including the proposed Palghar Deep Port, to enhance maritime infrastructure and trade;
(b) the details of port modernisation and connectivity projects undertaken during the last three years, project-wise;
(c) the investment sanctioned, released, and utilized, along with the additional cargo handling capacity created; and
(d) the expected impact of these initiatives, including the Palghar Deep Port project, on trade, exports, coastal shipping, logistics efficiency and employment generation in Maharashtra?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish manufacturing facilities for solar photovoltaic modules, advanced battery storage systems, green hydrogen equipment and allied renewable energy components in Maharashtra under various central schemes;
(b) the details of investment proposals received and approved, project-wise;
(c) the incentives, including Production Linked Incentive (PLI) and other central assistance, provided for such projects; and
(d) the employment likely to be generated and the expected contribution of these projects towards clean energy, domestic manufacturing, exports and energy security in Maharashtra?

(a) whether any institutional mechanism has been established to upgrade the Kolhapur foundry and allied engineering cluster, including GOSHIMA, SMAK and MSMEs in Shirol, for integration into the domestic Electric Vehicle (EV) component supply chain;
(b) whether financial assistance, green technology incentives or concessional credit have been provided under the Industrial Infrastructure Upgradation Scheme (IIUS) for adoption of sustainable electric casting systems; and
(c) the number of MSMEs in Kolhapur, Sangli and Ichalkaranji that have received technological upgradation support under the RAMP Programme and PMEGP for green manufacturing?

(a) the funds sanctioned, released and utilised under the UDAN Scheme for expansion, runway extension and night-landing facilities at Kolhapur airport;
(b) whether Government has examined the feasibility of introducing direct flights connecting Kolhapur with Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Delhi to promote trade, textile exports and tourism; and
(c) the measures taken to monitor and regulate excessive dynamic airfare pricing during peak festival seasons on routes serving western Maharashtra?

(a) whether Government has promoted industrial corridors, industrial nodes, logistics parks and investment projects in Maharashtra under various national industrial development programmes to strengthen manufacturing and exports;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned and their present status during the last five years, district-wise;
(c) the investment committed, funds released, private investment attracted and employment generated through these projects; and
(d) the expected contribution of these initiatives towards manufacturing growth, export competitiveness, MSME development and balanced regional industrial development in Maharashtra?

(a) whether Government has taken effective steps to promote natural farming, organic farming, micro-irrigation and climate-resilient agricultural practices in Maharashtra to enhance sustainable agriculture and reduce cultivation costs;
(b) the details of farmers covered under these initiatives during the last three years, district-wise;
(c) the funds sanctioned, released and utilized under the respective Central schemes, year-wise; and
(d) the impact of these interventions on input costs, crop productivity, water-use efficiency, soil health and farmers' income, particularly in drought-prone districts of the State?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the tourism development projects in Maharashtra, particularly in view of forthcoming Nashik Kumbh Mela;
(b) the details of tourism, pilgrimage, heritage and infrastructure projects sanctioned under various schemes in Maharashtra during the last five years, district-wise;
(c) the funds sanctioned, released and utilized for these projects, year-wise; and
(d) whether any special assistance has been proposed for infrastructure augmentation, pilgrim amenities, and employment generation in Nashik for the Mela and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken measures to strengthen One Stop Centres (OSCs) and women helplines in Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of centres functioning;
(c) the number of women assisted during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to improve access to legal, medical and counselling services?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the National Education Policy (NEP), 2020 in Maharashtra;
(b) the status of reforms introduced in school and higher education institutions in the State;
(c) the Central financial assistance released during the last three years; and
(d) the measures taken to improve learning outcomes, digital education and teacher training?

(a) whether Government proposes to strengthen pharmaceutical and bulk drug manufacturing in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned under Production Linked Incentive (PLI) and Bulk Drug Park schemes;
(c) the investment attracted and employment generated; and
(d) the steps taken to improve domestic production of essential medicines?

(a) the number of MSMEs registered in the State of Maharashtra during the last three years;
(b) the financial assistance, credit support and technology upgradation extended to MSMEs in the State;
(c) whether special measures have been taken to promote MSMEs in backward districts of Vidarbha and Marathwada; and
(d) the employment generated through these initiatives?

(a) whether Coal India Limited has undertaken Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) projects in coal mining districts of Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of expenditure incurred during the last three years;
(c) the sectors covered under these projects, including health, education and drinking water; and
(d) the mechanism adopted for monitoring the implementation and outcomes of such initiatives?

(a) whether Government has assessed the need for developing greenfield airports in underserved regions of the State of Maharashtra, particularly in Vidarbha and Marathwada;
(b) the details of proposals received from the State Government during the last three years;
(c) whether financial assistance has been extended for airport infrastructure and air navigation facilities; and
(d) the expected socio-economic benefits, including employment generation and tourism promotion, arising out of these proposed projects?

(a) whether Government has reviewed export performance of Maharashtra during the last three years;
(b) the details of exports, particularly from engineering, pharmaceuticals, agriculture and textiles, sector-wise;
(c) the initiatives undertaken to strengthen export infrastructure; and
(d) the measures taken to support exporters through logistics, market access and trade facilitation?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the telecom connectivity in rural and tribal areas of Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of villages provided with 4G/5G connectivity under the Central schemes;
(c) the funds released during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to bridge the digital divide?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) in Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of fisheries infrastructure projects sanctioned;
(c) the funds released and utilised; and
(d) the employment generated through these initiatives?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish new Central educational institutions, including Kendriya Vidyalayas, Navodaya Vidyalayas and Higher Educational Institutions in Maharashtra;
(b) the district-wise details of proposals received;
(c) the action taken thereon; and
(d) the timeline for approval and establishment of such institutions?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the availability of doctors, specialists and nursing staff in Central health institutions and Government-supported facilities in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of vacancies reported;
(c) the steps taken to fill these vacancies; and
(d) the measures adopted to strengthen healthcare services in rural and tribal districts?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the implementation of the National AYUSH Mission (NAM) in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of AYUSH hospitals, dispensaries and wellness centres established during the last three years, district-wise;
(c) the funds allocated and utilized for promoting Ayurveda, Yoga, Unani, Siddha and Homoeopathy in the State; and
(d) the steps taken to integrate AYUSH services with primary healthcare, particularly in tribal and rural areas of Maharashtra?

(a) whether Government proposes to strengthen solid waste management and sewage treatment infrastructure in urban local bodies of the State of Maharashtra;
(b) the details of financial assistance provided;
(c) the cities covered under these initiatives; and
(d) the expected impact on urban sanitation and environmental sustainability?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment regarding the expansion and modernization of airports in Maharashtra, particularly at Nagpur, Pune, Nashik, Kolhapur and Amravati, in view of increasing passenger and cargo traffic;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (UDAN) in the State, district-wise;
(c) whether any proposals are under consideration for improving air cargo facilities to promote exports from Maharashtra; and
(d) the timeline for completion of these projects and the funds allocated during the last three years?

(a) the details regarding the development of museums, libraries and other cultural infrastructure in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many new institutions have been established and how many existing ones have been upgraded or modernized;
(c) the measures being implemented to digitize archives, promote public engagement and facilitate educational programmes; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with State authorities to ensure accessibility, maintenance and community participation, thereby preserving historical artifacts, manuscripts and cultural knowledge, promoting learning and enhancing the State’s cultural identity and heritage for researchers, students and the general public?

(a) the details regarding the implementation of postal financial services and e-governance initiatives in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many beneficiaries have availed savings, insurance, pension and direct benefit transfer schemes through post offices;
(c) the steps being taken to integrate digital platforms, improve service delivery and enhance efficiency in postal operations; and
(d) how the Ministry coordinates with the State authorities to promote awareness, ensure transparency and strengthen rural and urban outreach, thereby leveraging postal networks to support financial inclusion, Government services and economic development across the State?

(a) details regarding welfare schemes for senior citizens in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) how many beneficiaries have received pensions, healthcare support, educational assistance and livelihood programs;
(c) what steps are being taken to ensure timely delivery of benefits, grievance redressal and increased awareness of schemes; and
(d) how does the Ministry coordinate with Maharashtra State authorities to promote social inclusion, capacity-building programs and targeted interventions that enhance the dignity, welfare and economic empowerment of senior citizens across rural and urban areas of the State?

(a) details regarding digital governance and e-Panchayat initiatives implemented in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many Gram Panchayats have been equipped with digital infrastructure for record-keeping, financial management and service delivery;
(c) what measures are being taken to train Panchayat officials and elected representatives in digital tools, online monitoring and grievance redressal systems; and
(d) how does the Ministry coordinate with Maharashtra State authorities to ensure effective utilization of technology, transparency in fund allocation and timely delivery of citizen-centric services through Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRI), thereby promoting good governance and rural development?

(a) details of major rural development schemes implemented in the State of Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) the number of villages and households that have benefited under programs such as PMGSY, MGNREGA, PMAY-G and watershed development schemes;
(c) the measures being taken to ensure timely fund release, quality execution and effective monitoring of projects; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with Maharashtra State authorities to address regional disparities, improve rural infrastructure, create sustainable employment and enhance the overall quality of life in rural and tribal areas of the State?

(a) the initiatives taken to strengthen cybersecurity, digital skills and innovation in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) the number of individuals who have been trained in emerging technologies such as Artificial Intelligence (AI), cybersecurity and cloud computing;
(c) the measures being taken to support research, Startups and innovation hubs in the electronics and IT sectors; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry collaborates with Government of Maharashtra, educational institutions and industry to enhance cyber resilience, promote innovation ecosystems and create sustainable employment opportunities in the rapidly evolving digital economy of the State?

(a) details regarding measures to prevent violence and protect women and children in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) how many support centres, helplines and rehabilitation programs have been established for victims of domestic violence, trafficking and child abuse;
(c) what steps are being taken to ensure awareness, legal support and timely intervention; and
(d) how does the Ministry coordinate with Maharashtra State authorities to strengthen community outreach, monitoring mechanisms and enforcement of laws, thereby safeguarding the rights, safety and well-being of women and children while promoting social justice and protection across the State?

(a) the details of wind energy initiatives in Maharashtra over the last five years, the installed capacity added and the new wind power projects or parks approved or commissioned in the State;
(b) the steps being taken to attract private investment, improve infrastructure and integrate wind energy with the State’s electricity grid; and
(c) the manner in which the Ministry is supporting research, training and technological innovation in wind energy and the measures being implemented to ensure sustainable development, environmental compliance and community participation in Maharashtra’s wind energy sector?

(a) the details of petroleum storage, refinery and import infrastructure located in the State of Maharashtra; 
(b) whether capacity augmentation or modernization projects are under implementation, and the role of such infrastructure in ensuring national energy security; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the employment and economic benefits arising from these projects in the State, and the steps taken to enhance safety, environmental compliance and disaster preparedness at petroleum installations in the State of Maharashtra?

(a) details of initiatives undertaken to develop food processing infrastructure in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) the number of food processing units, mega food parks, agro-processing clusters and cold chain facilities that have been established or upgraded in the State;
(c) the measures being taken to support farmers, food processors and entrepreneurs through financial assistance, technology adoption and market linkages; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with Maharashtra State authorities to reduce post-harvest losses, enhance value addition and generate employment while strengthening the food processing ecosystem across rural and urban regions of the State?

(a) the details of initiatives to promote professional and competitive sports in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many athletes have received scholarships, training support and exposure to national and international competitions;
(c) the measures being taken to develop Centres of Excellence to identify talent in rural and tribal areas and ensure scientific coaching and fitness support; and
(d) how the Ministry coordinates with the State authorities to enhance sports promotion, provide financial and infrastructural assistance and encourage participation in various disciplines, thereby improving the State’s performance in national and international sporting events and fostering a culture of sports excellence?

(a) details regarding education and skill development initiatives for tribal communities in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) how many students have received scholarships, vocational training and support for higher education;
(c) what measures are being implemented to improve school infrastructure, digital learning access and enrollment rates among tribal children; and
(d) how does the Ministry coordinate with Maharashtra State authorities to ensure inclusive education, bridge literacy gaps, provide employment-oriented skill training and enhance opportunities for youth from tribal areas, thereby promoting social mobility, empowerment and sustainable livelihoods for Maharashtra’s tribal population?

(a) details of initiatives undertaken to promote skill development in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many skill development centres, vocational training institutes and apprenticeship programs have been established or upgraded in the State;
(c) what steps are being taken to ensure access to training for youth in rural, tribal and under-served areas; and
(d) how does the Ministry coordinate with Maharashtra State authorities and industries to enhance employability, provide placement opportunities and promote entrepreneurship, ensuring that skill development programs effectively contribute to sustainable livelihoods and economic growth across the State?

(a) the details of initiatives to strengthen the healthcare workforce and medical education in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) the number of medical colleges, nursing institutes and skill development programs established or upgraded in the State;
(c) what measures are being taken to ensure adequate training, deployment and retention of doctors, nurses and allied health professionals, particularly in rural and remote areas; and
(d) how the Ministry supports Maharashtra in continuous medical education, telemedicine integration and research programs to improve healthcare quality, reduce regional disparities and enhance overall health outcomes?

(a) details of initiatives undertaken to promote the textile, handloom and powerloom sectors in Maharashtra over the last five years;
(b) the number of textile parks, common facility centers and modernization projects approved or implemented in the State;
(c) the measures being taken to support traditional weavers, artisans and small textile units through financial assistance, technology upgradation and market linkages; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with Maharashtra State authorities to generate employment, enhance productivity and strengthen Maharashtra’s position in the national and global textile value chain?

(a) the details regarding support provided to performing arts, music, dance and traditional arts in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) the number of artists who have received fellowships, grants and training opportunities;
(c) the steps being taken to preserve endangered art forms and promote cultural education; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with the State authorities to organize cultural festivals, workshops and competitions?

(a) the details of initiatives taken to expand and modernize postal services in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many new post offices have been opened and how many existing offices have been upgraded with digital facilities;
(c) the measures being taken to ensure timely mail delivery, improved financial services and greater accessibility in rural and remote areas; and
(d) how the Ministry coordinates with Maharashtra State authorities to promote awareness of postal schemes, integrate technology for efficiency and strengthen postal infrastructure to support e-commerce, financial inclusion and citizen services across the State?

(a) details of efforts to enhance road connectivity and infrastructure development in Kolhapur, Maharashtra, over the last three years;
(b) how many new bridges, bypasses and service roads have been constructed to improve intra-district and inter-State connectivity, what measures are being taken to support logistics, industrial transport and tourism through upgraded road networks; and
(c) how does the Ministry collaborate with Maharashtra State authorities to ensure sustainable road development, reduce congestion and improve maintenance practices, thereby promoting economic growth, employment opportunities and overall regional development in Kolhapur?

(a) details regarding rural development programs implemented through Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) in Maharashtra in the last five years;
(b) how many projects related to sanitation, water supply, road construction and community welfare have been sanctioned and completed under PRIs;
(c) what steps are being taken to ensure proper monitoring, transparency and accountability in project execution; and
(d) how does the Ministry support Maharashtra in building the technical and financial capacity of Panchayats, promoting participatory planning and integrating social welfare schemes to improve rural infrastructure, livelihoods and overall development outcomes across villages in the State?

(a) the details of measures taken by the Ministry to promote traditional systems of medicine, including Ayurveda, Yoga, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy (AYUSH), in Maharashtra;
(b) the number of AYUSH hospitals, wellness centres and training institutes established in the State in the last five years;
(c) the initiatives being implemented to raise public awareness, integrate AYUSH therapies into mainstream healthcare and support local practitioners; and
(d) the steps being taken to sustainably cultivate and utilise medicinal plants indigenous to Maharashtra to strengthen AYUSH services?

(a) whether Government proposes to expand and modernize Kolhapur airport in the State of Maharashtra to improve regional air connectivity;
(b) the present status of runway expansion, navigational aids and safety infrastructure at the airport;
(c) whether any timelines have been fixed for attracting additional airlines and destinations under the UDAN or other schemes; and
(d) the measures being taken to address operational challenges so as to ensure regular, affordable and reliable air services for passengers, businesses and tourists from the Kolhapur region?

(a) the status of projects sanctioned under AMRUT and AMRUT 2.0 in cities of the State of Maharashtra;
(b) the details of funds allocated, released and utilized for water supply, sewerage and drainage works;
(c) whether any projects have been delayed or revised; and
(d) further, the steps taken to address issues of project execution, coordination with urban local bodies and quality control and whether additional assistance is proposed to improve urban infrastructure in rapidly growing cities of the State of Maharashtra?

(a) the status of coal mining operations in the State of Maharashtra, particularly in Chandrapur, Nagpur and Yavatmal districts;
(b) whether environmental and forest clearance issues have affected production levels;
(c) the details of measures taken to balance coal extraction with environmental protection and rehabilitation of affected communities; and
(d) whether any mine closures or capacity reductions have been proposed and the steps taken to ensure compliance with environmental norms and sustainable mining practices in the State?

(a) whether Government has effectively implemented the One District One Product (ODOP) Districts as Export Hubs initiative in Maharashtra, with particular reference to Mumbai as the State’s principal export, logistics and financial hub;
(b) if so, role played by Central Government in supporting ODOP implementation across all 36 districts of Maharashtra and the extent to which Mumbai’s ports, airport and trade facilitation infrastructure have been leveraged; and
(c) the corrective measures, timelines and monitoring framework proposed to ensure balanced export growth across Maharashtra?

(a) details of initiatives undertaken to preserve and promote cultural heritage in Maharashtra during the last five years;
(b) how many heritage sites, monuments and traditional art forms have been restored, documented or promoted through central schemes;
(c) the measures being taken to support local artists, craftsmen and cultural organizations; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry coordinates with Maharashtra State authorities to organize festivals, exhibitions and awareness programmes that enhance public engagement, attract tourism and safeguard the State’s rich intangible and tangible cultural heritage for future generations?

(a) the details of the initiatives undertaken by the Ministry to strengthen fertilizer production and distribution infrastructure in Maharashtra, specifically the number of fertilizer manufacturing units, storage facilities and distribution centres established or upgraded in the State in the last five years;
(b) the measures being implemented to ensure timely availability of quality fertilizers to farmers, especially in rural and tribal areas; and
(c) the plan of Government to promote balanced and sustainable fertilizer use, support local industries and reduce dependency on imported raw materials?

(a) the details on research and innovation initiatives taken in Maharashtra to strengthen Ayush practices;
(b) specifically, what grants, collaborations with universities, clinical research projects and quality monitoring programs have been undertaken in the last five years;
(c) the manner in which the Ministry plans to enhance evidence-based Ayush therapies and ensure their safety and efficacy; and
(d) the measures introduced to improve access to Ayush healthcare in rural and tribal areas of Maharashtra and to promote employment opportunities for local Ayush practitioners?

(a) whether Government has assessed the current capacity and infrastructure constraints at major airports in the State of Maharashtra, particularly Mumbai, Pune, Nagpur and Aurangabad;
(b) whether congestion, slot saturation and passenger inconvenience have been reported at these airports;
(c) the details of steps taken or proposed to augment terminal capacity, runways and air traffic management systems; and
(d) whether Government plans to expedite greenfield airport projects and expansion under the UDAN and other schemes to improve regional air connectivity in the State of Maharashtra and if so, the timelines fixed for completion of such projects?

(a) the current status and growth trajectory of the textile sector in Maharashtra, including the number of textile units, employment generated and production capacity in the last three years;
(b) the contribution of Maharashtra’s textile industry to the overall GDP of the country, including exports of textiles and garments;
(c) the steps taken by Government to promote investment, technology upgradation, skill development and competitiveness of textile units in Maharashtra, particularly MSMEs; and
(d) the measures and timelines proposed by Government to strengthen Maharashtra’s textile sector, enhance its GDP contribution and improve exports, employment and industrial growth in the coming years?

(a) whether Government has taken effective steps to promote organic farming in Maharashtra, particularly through the implementation of Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY), if so, the details thereof;
(b) the total area brought under organic cultivation, the number of certified organic farmers and the district-wise distribution thereof in Maharashtra;
(c) the number of PKVY clusters sanctioned, funds released and utilised and the extent to which the prescribed assistance has actually reached farmers; and
(d) whether adequate training, demonstration and awareness programmes have been conducted through Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs), agricultural universities and NGOs?

(a) whether Government has formulated any new strategy to attract foreign tourists and boost tourism-led economic growth and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Maharashtra, despite having major tourism destinations such as Mumbai, Ajanta, Ellora, Konkan coast and religious circuits, has witnessed stagnation in foreign tourist inflows in recent years and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes specific international marketing campaigns, visa facilitation measures or infrastructure support to promote Maharashtra as a global tourism destination and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether consultations have been held with Government of Maharashtra to address these concerns and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has conducted any comprehensive scientific studies to evaluate the impact of rising sea levels, coastal erosion and climate-induced changes on coastal settlements across the country, particularly along the Maharashtra coastline;
(b) if so, the details and key findings of such assessments in respect of Maharashtra; and
(c) whether Government proposes to launch or expand any new initiatives in the State for long-term monitoring, sustainable coastal planning and community-based climate resilience to address the challenges posed by sea-level rise and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has implemented major central social welfare schemes, in the State of Maharashtra during the last three years;
(b) if so, the scheme-wise funds sanctioned, released and utilised, along with the number of beneficiaries covered, year-wise;
(c) the number of applications received and benefits sanctioned to Economically Weaker Sections, Scheduled Castes and Other Backward Classes in Maharashtra; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen social security for unorganised workers and migrant labourers in Maharashtra, including health coverage, portability of benefits and income support mechanisms?

(a) the details of solar park projects approved and developed in the State of Maharashtra under the Solar Park Scheme, indicating their locations, sanctioned capacity, operational capacity and present status of implementation;
(b) the total solar power capacity generated through operational solar parks in the State and the extent to which these parks have contributed to Maharashtra’s renewable energy targets under the National Solar Mission; and
(c) whether local communities, farmers and cooperatives are being adequately involved in solar park projects through land leasing, employment or revenue-sharing mechanisms and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik (UDAN) scheme in the country and in the State of Maharashtra since its inception, including the total number of routes operationalised and those that have become non-operational or discontinued, with reasons such as poor viability, low load factors and frequent service disruptions;
(b) whether UDAN version 5.4 has been launched and the manner in which it seeks to address persistent shortcomings of earlier rounds; and
(c) the number of routes and airports in the State of Maharashtra proposed to be covered under UDAN 5.4?

(a) whether Government has taken initiatives to promote sports and physical fitness in Maharashtra, including development of modern sports infrastructure, training academies, and grassroot talent identification programmes in urban and rural areas; 
(b) the steps being taken to encourage traditional and indigenous sports, increase participation of women and differently-abled athletes and provide scholarships or financial support to promising youth; and 
(c) the details of funds allocated, projects implemented, sports facilities upgraded, and achievements recorded in national and international competitions in the State during the last three years?

(a) objectives and scope of Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS) and manner in which it differs from other station redevelopment initiatives;
(b) total number of railway stations in Maharashtra identified under ABSS and the Station Redevelopment Programme, along with their names;
(c) current status of redevelopment work at these stations, including project cost, contractors/agencies and expected timelines;
(d) passenger amenities and infrastructure improvements being provided, such as roof plazas, waiting lounges, lifts, escalators and digital displays;
(e) funds allocated, released and utilized over last three years; and
(f) measures taken to address any delays, like land acquisition issues or coordination challenges?

(a) the criteria adopted for selecting 100 districts under the Pradhan Mantri Dhan Dhaan Krishi Yojana (PMDDKY);
(b) whether any districts from Maharashtra have been included in the initial phase, along with the components and nature of projects proposed in each district;
(c) whether the Yojana includes targeted interventions to help farmers shift from water-intensive or low-yield crops to sustainable, high-value crops in Maharashtra, if so, the details thereof;
(d) plans to establish cold storage, warehouses, or irrigation systems in drought-prone areas like Marathwada and Vidarbha; and
(e) steps to ensure participation of FPOs, women farmers, and Self-Help Groups in Maharashtra?

(a) the number of villages in Maharashtra connected under the BharatNet project;
(b) the timeline for providing high-speed internet to remaining areas;
(c) whether mobile connectivity has been strengthened in remote and tribal areas of the State; and
(d) the number of new telecom towers and 5G sites commissioned during the last two years?

(a) the number of schools and higher educational institutions in the State of Maharashtra benefitting under the Samagra Shiksha and RUSA schemes;
(b) whether any proposal exists to upgrade select Universities in the State as Centres of Excellence; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to improve immunization coverage among tribal children aged 0-5 years in Gujarat and Maharashtra, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the present immunization coverage among tribal children in those States, district-wise;
(c) the special campaigns, outreach initiatives or mobile health teams deployed in tribal areas under UIP or Mission Indradhanush;
(d) the challenges such as inaccessibility, hesitancy or shortage of health personnel and measures taken to address them;
(e) whether Government is collaborating with NGOs and the outcomes; and
(f) whether any audits or evaluations have been conducted in tribal areas and their findings?

(a) the passenger traffic handled by Maharashtra airports during the last three years;
(b) whether steps are being taken to enhance cargo and maintenance facilities in the State; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

